WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.501
Narrator: This is the home page of Marcelo Paiva's site, in Safari, with VoiceOver on.

2
00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:10.725
Narrator: I'm going to listen to it the way someone who can't see the screen would meet it.

3
00:00:11.347 --> 00:00:14.482
VoiceOver: Skip to content link is in the VoiceOver cursor

4
00:00:14.482 --> 00:00:16.560
Narrator: The goal of this test is simple.

5
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.108
Narrator: Can someone using VoiceOver understand this page, find what they need,

6
00:00:21.108 --> 00:00:23.707
Narrator: and use its controls, without seeing it?

7
00:00:24.108 --> 00:00:28.779
Narrator: I test in six steps. First, I inspect the page structure in the code.

8
00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:30.946
Narrator: Second, the keyboard on its own.

9
00:00:30.946 --> 00:00:35.008
Narrator: Third, a reading pass with the screen reader, top to bottom.

10
00:00:35.008 --> 00:00:40.492
Narrator: Fourth, jumping by headings, landmarks and links. Fifth, the controls themselves.

11
00:00:40.492 --> 00:00:43.133
Narrator: And sixth, real tasks, start to finish.

12
00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:48.097
Narrator: In this series, each step gets its own short video, on this same page.

13
00:00:48.097 --> 00:00:51.618
Narrator: Along the way I find a problem in one of its controls…

14
00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:55.009
Narrator: and the last video shows it fixed, and tested again.
